1
00:01:03,239 --> 00:01:04,242
Hey.

2
00:01:04,242 --> 00:01:06,453
What on earth did you do to me?

3
00:01:06,453 --> 00:01:08,705
What did I do? Don't be dramatic.

4
00:01:08,705 --> 00:01:11,563
This is my room. And my bed.

5
00:01:14,751 --> 00:01:16,962
This blanket is mine too.

6
00:01:37,692 --> 00:01:39,402
Hold on,

7
00:01:39,402 --> 00:01:41,279
what's my baby doing out here?

8
00:01:41,279 --> 00:01:42,489
Wait,

9
00:01:42,489 --> 00:01:45,513
we only opened one bottle, right?

10
00:01:52,726 --> 00:01:54,375
Sun Tae Hyung.

11
00:01:54,375 --> 00:01:58,338
There's one more I kept hidden.

12
00:01:58,338 --> 00:02:00,340
Now, it's my turn.

13
00:02:00,340 --> 00:02:01,549
Let's roll, baby.

14
00:02:01,549 --> 00:02:03,510
Pull yourself together, Tae Hyung.

15
00:02:03,510 --> 00:02:04,719
This lighting is gorgeous.

16
00:02:04,719 --> 00:02:06,179
That's my sister's, though...

17
00:02:06,179 --> 00:02:09,305
Pour me a drink.

18
00:02:09,305 --> 00:02:11,933
I'm having this much.

19
00:02:20,858 --> 00:02:24,489
Keep it down or the baby wakes up.

20
00:02:24,489 --> 00:02:26,991
Hold on, I'll snap one for you.

21
00:02:26,991 --> 00:02:28,952
- Am I doing it right?
- No.

22
00:02:28,952 --> 00:02:30,537
What an idiot, seriously.

23
00:02:30,537 --> 00:02:31,996
Wrong way. It's flipped around.

24
00:02:31,996 --> 00:02:33,039
Hold it this way instead.

25
00:02:33,039 --> 00:02:33,832
The heck is this?

26
00:02:33,832 --> 00:02:36,042
Steady it like this and shoot.

27
00:02:36,042 --> 00:02:37,962
Click.

28
00:02:39,254 --> 00:02:41,840
Keep your hands off my baby.

29
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:44,384
Want me to show you my award?

30
00:02:44,384 --> 00:02:47,095
As soon as I got into this field,

31
00:02:47,095 --> 00:02:47,971
everyone called me brilliant.

32
00:02:47,971 --> 00:02:50,744
Genius. Pure brilliance.

33
00:02:55,309 --> 00:02:56,563
[Grand Prize]
That's impressive.

34
00:02:56,563 --> 00:02:59,482
Check out this masterpiece.

35
00:02:59,482 --> 00:03:02,652
Hold on, those words came out of me?

36
00:03:02,652 --> 00:03:06,030
You got totally drunk
and lost it completely, huh?

37
00:03:06,030 --> 00:03:08,347
All of this chaos began with...

38
00:03:10,199 --> 00:03:12,662
I want to see my sister.

39
00:03:12,662 --> 00:03:13,872
It's okay, stop crying.

40
00:03:13,872 --> 00:03:16,480
Don't touch me.

41
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:19,878
You've got to be kidding.

42
00:03:19,878 --> 00:03:21,087
Did I seriously cry?

43
00:03:21,087 --> 00:03:21,796
I can't believe this.

44
00:03:21,796 --> 00:03:25,155
Why was I comforting you?

45
00:03:31,681 --> 00:03:33,789
I'm burning up.

46
00:03:40,148 --> 00:03:42,089
It's freezing.

47
00:03:46,154 --> 00:03:48,387
- No!
- No!

48
00:03:51,788 --> 00:03:53,912
[Episode 4]

49
00:03:53,912 --> 00:03:55,371
We should stop drinking for now.

50
00:03:55,371 --> 00:03:56,414
Actually,

51
00:03:56,414 --> 00:03:58,166
let's cut it out for good.

52
00:03:58,166 --> 00:04:00,043
This is terrible for Woo Joo.

53
00:04:00,043 --> 00:04:02,337
Why did you break out that cheap wine?

54
00:04:02,337 --> 00:04:03,630
Wine hits me way too hard.

55
00:04:03,630 --> 00:04:06,299
Who broke out fancy glasses for the mood?

56
00:04:06,299 --> 00:04:09,342
You got all hyped and flipped on the lights.

57
00:04:09,342 --> 00:04:10,845
You were complaining about the rain,

58
00:04:10,845 --> 00:04:12,639
so I tried to cheer you up.

59
00:04:12,639 --> 00:04:14,140
Then who said they actually like rain

60
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:16,434
and then cried like a baby?

61
00:04:16,434 --> 00:04:19,437
It always gets strange with you.

62
00:04:19,437 --> 00:04:21,606
I had zero desire to enter that room.

63
00:04:21,606 --> 00:04:23,942
That sounds really off.

64
00:04:23,942 --> 00:04:26,633
You walked into my room

65
00:04:27,902 --> 00:04:29,489
and stole my bed.

66
00:04:29,489 --> 00:04:31,532
Choose your words carefully.

67
00:04:31,532 --> 00:04:34,535
We just got wasted and fell asleep.

68
00:04:34,535 --> 00:04:36,518
Hey.

69
00:04:43,042 --> 00:04:45,046
The more we talk about it,

70
00:04:45,046 --> 00:04:47,507
the worse it gets.

71
00:04:47,507 --> 00:04:48,466
Starting today,

72
00:04:48,466 --> 00:04:50,551
there is

73
00:04:50,551 --> 00:04:52,136
no more alcohol. Period.

74
00:04:52,136 --> 00:04:53,388
Particularly

75
00:04:53,388 --> 00:04:56,079
when it rains. Not happening.

76
00:04:59,976 --> 00:05:02,077
Wrap this up by wiping the table.

77
00:06:03,164 --> 00:06:04,167
Excuse me?

78
00:06:04,167 --> 00:06:06,316
You actually slept with your in-law?

79
00:06:08,463 --> 00:06:11,716
Se Yeon, lower your voice.

80
00:06:11,716 --> 00:06:14,177
I said roommates, not bed partners!

81
00:06:14,177 --> 00:06:15,762
Have you lost your mind?

82
00:06:15,762 --> 00:06:18,681
We literally just slept. Nothing else.

83
00:06:18,681 --> 00:06:20,641
How many episodes did I miss here?

84
00:06:20,641 --> 00:06:22,143
That's moving at lightning speed.

85
00:06:22,143 --> 00:06:25,646
Living together and already into him?

86
00:06:25,646 --> 00:06:27,023
Right.

87
00:06:27,023 --> 00:06:28,775
The Pimang guy is kind of charming.

88
00:06:28,775 --> 00:06:30,151
Are you out of your mind?

89
00:06:30,151 --> 00:06:31,903
It was

90
00:06:31,903 --> 00:06:33,321
one hundred percent the drinks.

91
00:06:33,321 --> 00:06:35,698
No, the boiler is the real culprit.

92
00:06:35,698 --> 00:06:38,868
The first hot bath in ages wiped me out.

93
00:06:38,868 --> 00:06:40,370
And the alcohol went straight to my head.

94
00:06:40,370 --> 00:06:42,872
Was cohabiting with a guy a bad call?

95
00:06:42,872 --> 00:06:45,249
Since when are you so casual about hooking up?

96
00:06:45,249 --> 00:06:46,376
Are you serious right now?

97
00:06:46,376 --> 00:06:48,984
Nothing like that happened!

98
00:06:53,424 --> 00:06:55,510
Hyun Jin,

99
00:06:55,510 --> 00:06:58,185
that has to feel awkward now.

100
00:06:58,185 --> 00:06:58,930
Why would it be?

101
00:06:58,930 --> 00:07:02,642
One drunk night flips everything.

102
00:07:02,642 --> 00:07:06,646
So now do you see the in-law as a man?

103
00:07:06,646 --> 00:07:08,940
Absolutely not!

104
00:07:08,940 --> 00:07:11,734
That's the most absurd thing ever.

105
00:07:11,734 --> 00:07:13,945
Honestly?

106
00:07:13,945 --> 00:07:16,364
Go, go, he's wide open!

107
00:07:16,364 --> 00:07:17,073
Okay.

108
00:07:17,073 --> 00:07:18,324
There we go, there we go!

109
00:07:18,324 --> 00:07:19,450
Take the high side.

110
00:07:19,450 --> 00:07:20,451
- I've got the low end.
- Okay.

111
00:07:20,451 --> 00:07:21,452
Send it over.

112
00:07:21,452 --> 00:07:23,287
- Just touch it... Shoot!
- He's right below!

113
00:07:23,287 --> 00:07:24,288
Take the shot!

114
00:07:24,288 --> 00:07:25,623
Dude, just pull the trigger!

115
00:07:25,623 --> 00:07:28,000
How many times, man? Get it together.

116
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,317
Your head's not in the game today.

117
00:07:31,168 --> 00:07:32,255
What about Woo Joo?

118
00:07:32,255 --> 00:07:34,340
Her aunt has him since it's the weekend.

119
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:36,717
All organized, huh?

120
00:07:36,717 --> 00:07:38,636
Roommate life suits you?

121
00:07:38,636 --> 00:07:40,179
Pretty much, yeah.

122
00:07:40,179 --> 00:07:41,929
Give us the details on that setup.

123
00:07:41,929 --> 00:07:43,641
There's something I've been curious about.

124
00:07:43,641 --> 00:07:44,473
Like what?

125
00:07:44,473 --> 00:07:48,060
You guys live together.

126
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:50,646
After a shower, are you fully dressed?

127
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:52,775
You expect me to walk out bare?

128
00:07:52,775 --> 00:07:56,510
You two share shampoo and smell alike?

129
00:07:58,153 --> 00:07:59,699
You probably have the same scent.

130
00:07:59,699 --> 00:08:00,908
That's the dumbest thing I've...

131
00:08:00,908 --> 00:08:02,452
Coming here was a mistake. I'm out.

132
00:08:02,452 --> 00:08:03,453
Right?

133
00:08:03,453 --> 00:08:05,538
For real, it doesn't bother you at all?

134
00:08:05,538 --> 00:08:08,332
I mean, she's a woman and you're a man.

135
00:08:08,332 --> 00:08:10,168
Living that close,
feelings come out of nowhere...

136
00:08:10,168 --> 00:08:12,670
We're not that close, cut it out.

137
00:08:12,670 --> 00:08:17,114
She's so swamped I hardly see her.

138
00:08:18,342 --> 00:08:19,969
I'm leaving.

139
00:08:19,969 --> 00:08:20,636
Hey.

140
00:08:20,636 --> 00:08:22,763
What is it now?

141
00:08:22,763 --> 00:08:24,683
Is she good-looking?

142
00:08:27,224 --> 00:08:28,269
What?

143
00:08:28,269 --> 00:08:31,122
Is your in-law good-looking?

144
00:08:40,321 --> 00:08:42,365
Is she good-looking?

145
00:08:43,117 --> 00:08:45,037
No.

146
00:08:45,701 --> 00:08:47,912
Hi, Woo Joo.

147
00:08:52,919 --> 00:08:55,546
- You go fir--
- Go ahead.

148
00:08:55,546 --> 00:08:56,839
All right, I'll head in first.

149
00:08:56,839 --> 00:08:58,759
Sure.

150
00:09:21,904 --> 00:09:23,115
Hyun Jin, what's your problem?

151
00:09:23,115 --> 00:09:24,492
Why does he make you nervous?

152
00:09:24,492 --> 00:09:26,953
Are you out of your mind?

153
00:09:26,953 --> 00:09:28,977
I think I'm going crazy.

154
00:09:56,899 --> 00:10:00,675
You two share shampoo and smell alike?

155
00:10:02,697 --> 00:10:05,013
Excuse me.

156
00:10:06,323 --> 00:10:07,325
What?

157
00:10:07,325 --> 00:10:08,953
Well...

158
00:10:08,953 --> 00:10:10,371
Mind if I step in real quick?

159
00:10:10,371 --> 00:10:12,665
Are you crazy? I'm in the shower

160
00:10:12,665 --> 00:10:14,208
with nothing on right now.

161
00:10:14,208 --> 00:10:16,210
My bad. So sorry.

162
00:10:16,210 --> 00:10:18,693
She must have lost her mind.

163
00:10:24,484 --> 00:10:25,760
Come on, Tae Hyung.

164
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:27,247
What's wrong with you? Why so aware?

165
00:10:27,247 --> 00:10:27,972
What are you, twelve?

166
00:10:27,972 --> 00:10:29,432
It's not like you've never been with someone.

167
00:10:29,432 --> 00:10:32,184
Making a big deal out of nothing...

168
00:10:32,184 --> 00:10:33,728
Are you almost done?

169
00:10:33,728 --> 00:10:35,563
What's taking so long?

170
00:10:35,563 --> 00:10:37,671
All finished, heading out now.

171
00:10:38,274 --> 00:10:40,590
Why does she keep rushing me...

172
00:11:05,968 --> 00:11:07,909
Man, it's sweltering in here.

173
00:11:13,309 --> 00:11:15,333
This window is stuck.

174
00:11:17,102 --> 00:11:20,149
You press it like this

175
00:11:20,149 --> 00:11:22,257
and then push.

176
00:11:34,163 --> 00:11:38,189
Is your in-law good-looking?

177
00:11:47,426 --> 00:11:49,618
Is she good-looking?

178
00:11:52,723 --> 00:11:54,748
Is she good-looking?

179
00:12:12,616 --> 00:12:14,284
Hey.

180
00:12:14,284 --> 00:12:15,246
Hey.

181
00:12:15,246 --> 00:12:17,166
Yeah?

182
00:12:21,752 --> 00:12:24,213
The landlord still won't answer?

183
00:12:24,213 --> 00:12:27,158
This door needs to be repaired too.

184
00:12:30,175 --> 00:12:32,638
This one's broken too?

185
00:12:32,638 --> 00:12:34,558
Step outside for a sec.

186
00:12:45,776 --> 00:12:47,759
Do you see him as a man?

187
00:12:49,111 --> 00:12:51,197
Do you see him as a man?

188
00:13:01,582 --> 00:13:03,709
Do you see him as a man?

189
00:13:14,180 --> 00:13:15,639
Hey.

190
00:13:15,639 --> 00:13:17,559
Hey.

191
00:13:19,798 --> 00:13:22,605
Water costs a fortune these days.

192
00:13:22,605 --> 00:13:24,815
Let me give the landlord a ring.

193
00:13:24,815 --> 00:13:27,628
Isn't that right, Woo Joo?

194
00:13:36,535 --> 00:13:39,330
Since you just started
you wouldn't have a clue,

195
00:13:39,330 --> 00:13:43,167
but GloMarket holds
a seriously sore spot for our manager.

196
00:13:43,167 --> 00:13:45,544
Among every single project he's done,

197
00:13:45,544 --> 00:13:47,546
it's the one and only flop on his record.

198
00:13:47,546 --> 00:13:50,633
He even flew out to the U.S. headquarters
to meet with the CEO.

199
00:13:50,633 --> 00:13:51,801
Right at the last round,

200
00:13:51,801 --> 00:13:53,803
they turned him away
claiming Asian products couldn't hold

201
00:13:53,803 --> 00:13:55,638
their own in the market.

202
00:13:55,638 --> 00:13:56,514
In your case,

203
00:13:56,514 --> 00:13:58,015
when your contract runs out,
you just walk away,

204
00:13:58,015 --> 00:14:00,184
so I suppose the stakes
don't feel the same to you.

205
00:14:00,184 --> 00:14:02,061
Those of us on permanent staff

206
00:14:02,061 --> 00:14:05,231
are the ones left picking up the pieces.

207
00:14:05,231 --> 00:14:06,774
Moving on,

208
00:14:06,774 --> 00:14:09,631
you're seriously not the lobby girl, right?

209
00:14:10,736 --> 00:14:13,072
If you say you're not, I'll believe you, but...

210
00:14:13,072 --> 00:14:14,782
How does that add up though?

211
00:14:14,782 --> 00:14:17,034
Seriously, what kind of person
drags their husband

212
00:14:17,034 --> 00:14:18,619
and baby into the workplace?

213
00:14:18,619 --> 00:14:20,725
That's absolutely insane.

214
00:14:22,496 --> 00:14:25,626
Well, maybe she had

215
00:14:25,626 --> 00:14:27,378
something really urgent going on?

216
00:14:27,378 --> 00:14:30,653
People all have their own situations...

217
00:14:32,304 --> 00:14:34,218
Everybody does.

218
00:14:34,218 --> 00:14:35,719
They obviously have zero sense of boundaries.

219
00:14:35,719 --> 00:14:38,679
That dad in particular.

220
00:14:38,679 --> 00:14:40,931
Right?

221
00:14:40,931 --> 00:14:42,393
So let's be careful

222
00:14:42,393 --> 00:14:44,520
that we never get in the way

223
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:47,189
of our manager's project, got it?

224
00:14:47,189 --> 00:14:49,233
Absolutely.

225
00:14:49,233 --> 00:14:51,360
Forget a husband,

226
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:53,571
I can't even find a boyfriend.

227
00:14:53,571 --> 00:14:55,614
Good.

228
00:14:55,614 --> 00:14:57,867
Let's move to the meeting room.

229
00:14:57,867 --> 00:15:00,517
- Sure.
- Okay.

230
00:15:05,956 --> 00:15:10,335
[BS Food]

231
00:15:10,335 --> 00:15:11,338
Thrilling, isn't it?

232
00:15:11,338 --> 00:15:14,466
There's nothing like reclaiming
what slipped through our fingers.

233
00:15:14,466 --> 00:15:17,469
Let's seize the GloMarket.

234
00:15:17,469 --> 00:15:19,805
I need a full rundown of rival products
already on GloMarket,

235
00:15:19,805 --> 00:15:21,640
along with a game plan for taking them on.

236
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:23,267
The existing proposal needs
a complete overhaul too.

237
00:15:23,267 --> 00:15:25,394
Also, Hyun Jin.

238
00:15:25,394 --> 00:15:28,022
I'd like to see your work on organizing
the overseas distribution data.

239
00:15:28,022 --> 00:15:29,356
I actually prepared something

240
00:15:29,356 --> 00:15:31,150
just in case it came in handy.

241
00:15:31,150 --> 00:15:31,942
[GloMarket Platform Strategy]
On top of that,

242
00:15:31,942 --> 00:15:34,028
I've put together a report
on the latest shifts in consumer trends

243
00:15:34,028 --> 00:15:37,220
and a GloMarket sales analysis.

244
00:15:43,746 --> 00:15:44,955
Head over to my desk so we can

245
00:15:44,955 --> 00:15:47,103
jump right into this, Hyun Jin.

246
00:16:06,352 --> 00:16:07,895
Using this as a foundation,

247
00:16:07,895 --> 00:16:11,231
how about you try putting together
the first draft of the proposal?

248
00:16:11,231 --> 00:16:12,368
What?

249
00:16:12,368 --> 00:16:13,484
Me?

250
00:16:13,484 --> 00:16:16,570
I'm curious to see your approach
to the localization concepts as well.

251
00:16:16,570 --> 00:16:18,499
Is that overwhelming?

252
00:16:20,532 --> 00:16:23,474
No, I can do it.

253
00:16:25,704 --> 00:16:27,122
Goal!

254
00:16:27,122 --> 00:16:29,272
Here, you try too.

255
00:16:32,252 --> 00:16:34,588
Excuse me, mister.

256
00:16:34,588 --> 00:16:36,256
Mister in unit 207.

257
00:16:36,256 --> 00:16:38,300
Yeah, what do you want?

258
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:40,803
You have no clue

259
00:16:40,803 --> 00:16:43,681
how freaked out I've been because of you.

260
00:16:43,681 --> 00:16:46,080
Oh, darn it.

261
00:16:46,684 --> 00:16:49,061
Oh, gosh.

262
00:16:49,061 --> 00:16:51,230
If my in-law finds out, she's going to lose it.

263
00:16:51,230 --> 00:16:53,150
Hey, mister...

264
00:16:53,857 --> 00:16:56,527
Why are you blaming me for that?

265
00:16:56,527 --> 00:17:00,114
The boiler was busted from the start.

266
00:17:00,114 --> 00:17:01,073
You scared me!

267
00:17:01,073 --> 00:17:03,492
Didn't I warn you to stop
tossing your cigarette butts

268
00:17:03,492 --> 00:17:04,493
in the bottle?

269
00:17:04,493 --> 00:17:06,120
Those are from ages ago.

270
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:08,789
I quit smoking already.

271
00:17:08,789 --> 00:17:10,958
What? You can't even believe your own son?

272
00:17:10,958 --> 00:17:12,084
Hello.

273
00:17:12,084 --> 00:17:13,585
- How are you doing?
- Oh, I'm great.

274
00:17:13,585 --> 00:17:15,462
I have a report to make.

275
00:17:15,462 --> 00:17:18,090
Yesterday at roughly 5:32 p.m.,

276
00:17:18,090 --> 00:17:19,967
I spotted this gentleman right here

277
00:17:19,967 --> 00:17:23,326
puffing on a cigarette
outside the corner store.

278
00:17:25,305 --> 00:17:28,706
You're in big trouble when we get home.

279
00:17:29,893 --> 00:17:31,812
Don't you know the bro code?

280
00:17:31,812 --> 00:17:33,188
Bro code? Between us?

281
00:17:33,188 --> 00:17:34,815
You cost me a million won.

282
00:17:34,815 --> 00:17:36,025
Wait, a million won?

283
00:17:36,025 --> 00:17:37,317
What are you talking about, a million won?

284
00:17:37,317 --> 00:17:39,445
The boiler in this unit costs a million...

285
00:17:39,445 --> 00:17:40,320
Oh dear, what a nightmare!

286
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:41,363
A million won gone just like that

287
00:17:41,363 --> 00:17:43,115
and the landlord doesn't
even answer my calls...

288
00:17:43,115 --> 00:17:45,617
Come to think of it, that landlord seems

289
00:17:45,617 --> 00:17:47,661
like either the busiest person alive

290
00:17:47,661 --> 00:17:50,164
or someone who flat-out ignores calls.

291
00:17:50,164 --> 00:17:51,248
He'll answer sooner or later.

292
00:17:51,248 --> 00:17:52,624
Just tell the landlord to cover it. Easy fix.

293
00:17:52,624 --> 00:17:54,710
- Oh, that would work.
- Right.

294
00:17:54,710 --> 00:17:57,588
Hey, where's your other half?

295
00:17:57,588 --> 00:17:58,756
Huh?

296
00:17:58,756 --> 00:18:00,758
Your other half is right over there.

297
00:18:00,758 --> 00:18:02,384
Sir, keep your mouth shut.

298
00:18:02,384 --> 00:18:03,719
Right.

299
00:18:03,719 --> 00:18:05,471
Oh, you made it, sweetie?

300
00:18:05,471 --> 00:18:07,181
Hello.

301
00:18:07,181 --> 00:18:08,849
Sweetie?

302
00:18:08,849 --> 00:18:10,809
What?

303
00:18:10,809 --> 00:18:13,062
He says the two of you

304
00:18:13,062 --> 00:18:14,855
are super lovey-dovey.

305
00:18:14,855 --> 00:18:16,106
That's what you said, wasn't it?

306
00:18:16,106 --> 00:18:17,941
Mind your own business.

307
00:18:17,941 --> 00:18:21,403
Anyway, did you two eat yet?

308
00:18:21,403 --> 00:18:23,489
I just have to throw on a couple more plates,

309
00:18:23,489 --> 00:18:25,866
so come join us if you're hungry.

310
00:18:25,866 --> 00:18:26,867
And, well,

311
00:18:26,867 --> 00:18:29,912
if there's anything you need help with,
just say the word.

312
00:18:29,912 --> 00:18:31,205
Sure.

313
00:18:31,205 --> 00:18:32,081
- Got it.
- Bye.

314
00:18:32,081 --> 00:18:33,248
Thank you. We'll head home now.

315
00:18:33,248 --> 00:18:34,666
Sure, get home safe.

316
00:18:34,666 --> 00:18:36,585
Ask the landlord for compensation.

317
00:18:36,585 --> 00:18:37,586
Sleep tight, little one.

318
00:18:37,586 --> 00:18:38,879
That's how you grow up big and strong.

319
00:18:38,879 --> 00:18:39,838
Lovey-dovey.

320
00:18:39,838 --> 00:18:41,758
Mister, please.

321
00:18:42,424 --> 00:18:44,218
How does something like that even happen?

322
00:18:44,218 --> 00:18:45,219
Woo Joo's parents

323
00:18:45,219 --> 00:18:48,202
were genuinely wonderful people.

324
00:18:49,264 --> 00:18:52,707
The world can be so unfair.

325
00:18:54,770 --> 00:18:57,981
Death doesn't pick and choose

326
00:18:57,981 --> 00:18:59,922
between the good and the bad.

327
00:19:00,982 --> 00:19:03,277
You know that too.

328
00:19:08,075 --> 00:19:09,743
Hey.

329
00:19:09,743 --> 00:19:13,539
Did you go around saying
something strange about us?

330
00:19:13,539 --> 00:19:16,397
What's all that lovey-dovey talk
out of nowhere?

331
00:19:17,042 --> 00:19:18,085
What?

332
00:19:18,085 --> 00:19:23,029
I think he said that
just because you look so adorable.

333
00:19:30,097 --> 00:19:32,015
Yes, manager.

334
00:19:32,015 --> 00:19:34,476
Oh, right.

335
00:19:34,476 --> 00:19:35,561
I'll pull it all together

336
00:19:35,561 --> 00:19:37,312
and have it over to you in 20 minutes.

337
00:19:37,312 --> 00:19:38,772
Don't forget to attach
the lead time calculation

338
00:19:38,772 --> 00:19:40,691
with the initial proposal.

339
00:19:40,691 --> 00:19:43,193
Yes, that file you shared with me earlier...

340
00:19:43,193 --> 00:19:45,088
I should have it somewhere.

341
00:19:50,407 --> 00:19:51,410
Are you outside?

342
00:19:51,410 --> 00:19:52,536
Then let's talk later...

343
00:19:52,536 --> 00:19:54,621
No, I'm definitely at home.

344
00:19:55,495 --> 00:19:57,968
Was that a cat?

345
00:19:57,968 --> 00:20:00,023
Oh, be careful.

346
00:20:01,003 --> 00:20:03,088
The TV volume is way up, isn't it?

347
00:20:03,088 --> 00:20:07,259
I have trouble focusing
unless there's white noise on.

348
00:20:07,259 --> 00:20:10,262
Anyway, I'll have it all sorted
and sent your way.

349
00:20:10,262 --> 00:20:12,306
All right.

350
00:20:12,306 --> 00:20:14,766
If anything trips you up, reach out.

351
00:20:14,766 --> 00:20:17,583
Sure thing, manager.

352
00:20:22,149 --> 00:20:24,276
What's making you so jumpy?

353
00:20:24,276 --> 00:20:25,777
Is your manager that intimidating?

354
00:20:25,777 --> 00:20:27,697
It's not that.

355
00:20:28,570 --> 00:20:30,616
I have to show what I'm capable of.

356
00:20:30,616 --> 00:20:32,618
He put his faith in me
and handed me this opportunity,

357
00:20:32,618 --> 00:20:34,620
so I need to pour everything I have into this

358
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:36,914
and deliver real results.

359
00:20:36,914 --> 00:20:38,980
Prove yourself to who...

360
00:20:41,501 --> 00:20:43,128
Well...

361
00:20:43,128 --> 00:20:46,632
No shortage of people I need to impress.

362
00:20:46,632 --> 00:20:47,799
And beyond that,

363
00:20:47,799 --> 00:20:50,636
I'm the sole contract employee on this team,

364
00:20:50,636 --> 00:20:51,553
so even if I work myself to death,

365
00:20:51,553 --> 00:20:55,263
I don't know if I can survive.

366
00:20:55,263 --> 00:20:56,767
So,

367
00:20:56,767 --> 00:20:59,519
for a while,

368
00:20:59,519 --> 00:21:01,939
I'm going to be stuck
at the office late every night,

369
00:21:01,939 --> 00:21:04,111
so, if it's not too much to ask...

370
00:21:07,194 --> 00:21:10,113
just until this project wraps up,

371
00:21:10,113 --> 00:21:13,388
would you mind looking after Woo Joo for me?

372
00:21:17,285 --> 00:21:19,289
Okay.

373
00:21:19,289 --> 00:21:20,249
Honestly, it's fine.

374
00:21:20,249 --> 00:21:24,233
The two of us could benefit from
a little breathing room right now anyway.

375
00:21:26,255 --> 00:21:28,487
You get some rest too.

376
00:22:04,180 --> 00:22:06,506
Were you up all night?

377
00:22:16,452 --> 00:22:19,394
Have you been feeding yourself at all?

378
00:22:36,906 --> 00:22:40,703
Your auntie's working so hard to make it...

379
00:22:47,941 --> 00:22:51,801
She was actually kind of cute back then.

380
00:23:07,062 --> 00:23:10,713
[Pull your own weight, Hyun Jin!]

381
00:23:23,953 --> 00:23:25,729
You know what?

382
00:23:25,729 --> 00:23:29,505
I usually love rainy days.

383
00:23:49,062 --> 00:23:52,191
What are you pulling that off for?

384
00:23:56,736 --> 00:23:59,104
Have you ever experienced life
in a basement apartment?

385
00:23:59,104 --> 00:24:02,538
Do you know what street life is like?

386
00:24:03,432 --> 00:24:06,310
Do you have a clue about the story

387
00:24:06,310 --> 00:24:08,854
behind those glow-in-the-dark stars?

388
00:24:08,854 --> 00:24:10,708
When my sister and I were kids,

389
00:24:10,708 --> 00:24:14,318
we lived in this basement unit

390
00:24:14,318 --> 00:24:17,799
that flooded whenever it rained.

391
00:24:17,799 --> 00:24:20,116
So each rainy season,

392
00:24:20,116 --> 00:24:22,701
mold would spread all over the place,

393
00:24:22,701 --> 00:24:25,746
and no matter how hard we scrubbed,
it never went away.

394
00:24:25,746 --> 00:24:28,541
And you know what her solution was?

395
00:24:28,541 --> 00:24:30,167
My sister

396
00:24:30,167 --> 00:24:33,212
turned finding the mold into a little game

397
00:24:33,212 --> 00:24:37,591
and covered each spot
with glow-in-the-dark stars.

398
00:24:37,591 --> 00:24:39,718
It was

399
00:24:39,718 --> 00:24:42,680
so magical back then.

400
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:45,872
That explains why you always avoided

401
00:24:46,475 --> 00:24:48,395
this room.

402
00:24:50,438 --> 00:24:52,629
Because it reminds you of her.

403
00:24:54,859 --> 00:24:58,635
I wondered why you slept in the living room
when you had a good room.

404
00:25:06,620 --> 00:25:08,372
Whenever it rained,

405
00:25:08,372 --> 00:25:11,375
my sister would show up for me.

406
00:25:11,375 --> 00:25:13,358
And

407
00:25:14,253 --> 00:25:17,173
every time I broke down

408
00:25:17,173 --> 00:25:19,383
because I missed Mom,

409
00:25:20,468 --> 00:25:25,222
my sister would whip up some pancakes.

410
00:25:25,222 --> 00:25:29,040
She'd throw in corn and cheese
and all sorts of stuff.

411
00:25:32,396 --> 00:25:34,273
At that time, my sister was just

412
00:25:34,273 --> 00:25:36,817
fifteen years old.

413
00:25:39,737 --> 00:25:41,886
She sounds like a wonderful sister.

414
00:25:43,699 --> 00:25:46,307
But the very last words

415
00:25:47,077 --> 00:25:49,686
I ever spoke to that incredible person were

416
00:25:51,624 --> 00:25:55,169
"I don't want to be your sister anymore."

417
00:25:55,169 --> 00:25:57,213
In this exact room.

418
00:25:57,963 --> 00:26:00,613
What a horrible thing for me to say.

419
00:26:02,635 --> 00:26:05,179
And now

420
00:26:05,179 --> 00:26:09,141
I don't even have anyone to shelter me anymore,

421
00:26:11,644 --> 00:26:15,378
and I'm never going to taste
my sister's cooking again...

422
00:26:27,868 --> 00:26:30,329
I want to see her so badly...

423
00:26:46,762 --> 00:26:48,847
Have your meal with Bunny.

424
00:26:48,847 --> 00:26:51,308
There you go, don't stop eating.

425
00:26:51,308 --> 00:26:53,228
Wipe your hands.

426
00:26:57,731 --> 00:26:59,923
Oh no, it burned.

427
00:27:01,277 --> 00:27:03,343
It's raining a lot out there...

428
00:27:06,884 --> 00:27:07,908
Hey, little one.

429
00:27:07,908 --> 00:27:08,534
Yeah?

430
00:27:08,534 --> 00:27:09,743
Do you miss your auntie?

431
00:27:09,743 --> 00:27:11,328
With all this rain,
you just can't stop worrying, right?

432
00:27:11,328 --> 00:27:12,955
How about we try calling her?

433
00:27:12,955 --> 00:27:14,875
Yeah.

434
00:27:15,749 --> 00:27:19,336
You're the one who wanted to, okay?

435
00:27:21,171 --> 00:27:23,424
Yeah.

436
00:27:23,424 --> 00:27:25,801
I just got out of a meeting.

437
00:27:25,801 --> 00:27:27,886
Did you have dinner yet?

438
00:27:27,886 --> 00:27:28,846
There's this spot right by my work

439
00:27:28,846 --> 00:27:30,514
that does incredible kimchi fried rice.

440
00:27:30,514 --> 00:27:31,682
I'll grab some on my way back.

441
00:27:31,682 --> 00:27:33,642
The deluxe version with ham.

442
00:27:33,642 --> 00:27:35,603
I should make it home by eight or so.

443
00:27:35,603 --> 00:27:38,624
We'll just have something at home.

444
00:27:38,624 --> 00:27:40,357
Forget about that and just get here quick.

445
00:27:40,357 --> 00:27:42,151
So you would make it by eight?

446
00:27:42,151 --> 00:27:43,694
Hyun Jin.

447
00:27:43,694 --> 00:27:45,654
Did you go over the competitor pricing?

448
00:27:45,654 --> 00:27:47,573
Your figures didn't add up.

449
00:27:47,573 --> 00:27:48,407
Yes.

450
00:27:48,407 --> 00:27:51,160
I'll correct it and get it to you immediately.

451
00:27:53,078 --> 00:27:55,414
I'll call you back.

452
00:27:55,414 --> 00:27:57,334
Seriously...

453
00:27:58,250 --> 00:28:00,942
I put so much effort
into these kimchi pancakes...

454
00:28:09,197 --> 00:28:13,034
Sorry. It looks like
I'll be delayed a bit longer.

455
00:28:13,034 --> 00:28:15,579
What time will you get here?

456
00:28:15,579 --> 00:28:17,520
Delayed a bit longer?

457
00:28:19,290 --> 00:28:22,128
You're still at the office?

458
00:28:24,837 --> 00:28:26,631
I'll be there in 30 minutes.

459
00:28:26,631 --> 00:28:28,030
I need to get going.

460
00:28:28,030 --> 00:28:29,198
Have a safe trip home.

461
00:28:29,198 --> 00:28:31,325
Have a good one.

462
00:28:34,370 --> 00:28:36,290
Let's call it a day.

463
00:28:36,914 --> 00:28:38,874
Sure.

464
00:28:38,874 --> 00:28:40,751
It's raining, so I'll give you a ride.

465
00:28:40,751 --> 00:28:43,379
No, thank you. I'm fine.

466
00:28:43,379 --> 00:28:46,841
Do you and your sister still share a place?

467
00:28:47,633 --> 00:28:50,844
No, I live alone.

468
00:28:50,844 --> 00:28:53,555
There are some personal circumstances...

469
00:28:53,555 --> 00:28:56,225
We're heading to the same spot
as last time, correct?

470
00:28:56,225 --> 00:28:58,310
Seriously, you don't have to do this.

471
00:28:58,310 --> 00:29:01,897
The strategy in your proposal was off.

472
00:29:01,897 --> 00:29:03,857
I'll go over it with you on the way

473
00:29:03,857 --> 00:29:05,860
to be more efficient.

474
00:29:13,719 --> 00:29:15,744
This is just basic human decency.

475
00:29:15,744 --> 00:29:17,454
It's humanity, compassion,

476
00:29:17,454 --> 00:29:19,748
or more formally, "benevolence."

477
00:29:19,748 --> 00:29:21,458
You'll get it when you're older.

478
00:29:21,458 --> 00:29:22,584
Watch and learn from me.

479
00:29:22,584 --> 00:29:24,169
What about me?

480
00:29:24,169 --> 00:29:25,671
Look, this is for your sake.

481
00:29:25,671 --> 00:29:28,966
If your aunt gets sick,
you're the one who'll catch it.

482
00:29:28,966 --> 00:29:30,676
Your immune system is still weak.

483
00:29:30,676 --> 00:29:33,095
If you get sick, I'm the one

484
00:29:33,095 --> 00:29:33,762
who'll struggle.

485
00:29:33,762 --> 00:29:36,056
- Yes.
- Right.

486
00:29:36,056 --> 00:29:37,975
It seems like we're on the same page today.

487
00:29:37,975 --> 00:29:42,085
Since it's coming down out there,

488
00:29:43,188 --> 00:29:45,755
you need to...

489
00:29:46,794 --> 00:29:48,402
What brings you by?

490
00:29:48,402 --> 00:29:50,612
Oh, hello there, Woo Joo.

491
00:29:50,612 --> 00:29:51,613
Oh my.

492
00:29:51,613 --> 00:29:53,657
The baby's aunt left

493
00:29:53,657 --> 00:29:55,576
without an umbrella,

494
00:29:55,576 --> 00:29:58,620
so I'm going to bring it to her
out of a sense of humanity.

495
00:29:58,620 --> 00:30:00,622
No one is stopping you.

496
00:30:00,622 --> 00:30:02,332
I'll keep an eye on the baby,

497
00:30:02,332 --> 00:30:03,250
so you go on.

498
00:30:03,250 --> 00:30:04,585
Come on, play with me.

499
00:30:04,585 --> 00:30:06,211
- I appreciate it.
- Just get going already.

500
00:30:06,211 --> 00:30:09,423
He usually stays calm
when he has this stuffed animal.

501
00:30:09,423 --> 00:30:10,966
Gosh.

502
00:30:10,966 --> 00:30:12,593
This is quite charming.

503
00:30:12,593 --> 00:30:13,761
What's the plan?

504
00:30:13,761 --> 00:30:16,764
Are you leaving the baby to go pick her up?

505
00:30:16,764 --> 00:30:17,848
Mom.

506
00:30:17,848 --> 00:30:18,974
I got it.

507
00:30:18,974 --> 00:30:20,976
That hurts.

508
00:30:33,717 --> 00:30:35,532
[Do you have an umbrella with you?]

509
00:30:35,532 --> 00:30:37,910
When on earth is she coming?

510
00:30:42,915 --> 00:30:46,190
It's always a stroke of misfortune
when it rains.

511
00:30:55,052 --> 00:30:57,869
Oh, that's a nice car.

512
00:31:01,183 --> 00:31:03,894
Why is he so tall?

513
00:31:17,407 --> 00:31:19,493
I'm grateful for your help every time.

514
00:31:19,493 --> 00:31:20,536
You should head in.

515
00:31:20,536 --> 00:31:23,872
No, you go ahead first, Senior.

516
00:31:23,872 --> 00:31:27,584
Actually, I should say Manager...

517
00:31:27,584 --> 00:31:30,003
I need to use your title,

518
00:31:30,003 --> 00:31:32,069
but it's hard to break the habit.

519
00:31:52,693 --> 00:31:54,987
You'll end up sick again.

520
00:31:54,987 --> 00:31:56,907
Get home quickly.

521
00:32:23,557 --> 00:32:25,309
I worried for nothing.

522
00:32:25,309 --> 00:32:27,394
She should've mentioned the car ride.

523
00:32:27,394 --> 00:32:29,062
It's frustrating.

524
00:32:29,062 --> 00:32:29,771
That was a nice car.

525
00:32:29,771 --> 00:32:31,691
Hey.

526
00:32:46,872 --> 00:32:50,667
How long have you been waiting there?

527
00:32:50,667 --> 00:32:53,921
I honestly didn't expect you
to greet me outside.

528
00:32:53,921 --> 00:32:56,173
You claimed you had no one
to shield you from the rain,

529
00:32:56,173 --> 00:32:57,090
but you have many.

530
00:32:57,090 --> 00:32:58,717
You're even being driven home.

531
00:32:58,717 --> 00:33:00,969
The Manager suggested giving me a lift

532
00:33:00,969 --> 00:33:02,137
since the downpour was so heavy.

533
00:33:02,137 --> 00:33:04,640
Why did he give you a ride?

534
00:33:04,640 --> 00:33:06,058
Plus, why did you choose
to get off at that spot?

535
00:33:06,058 --> 00:33:07,100
You don't even have an umbrella,

536
00:33:07,100 --> 00:33:09,978
so you should've had him pull up to the door.

537
00:33:12,541 --> 00:33:14,191
It's a slightly complicated situation...

538
00:33:14,191 --> 00:33:16,652
I have zero interest
in hearing your explanation.

539
00:33:16,652 --> 00:33:18,572
None.

540
00:33:38,966 --> 00:33:41,218
Please stop making empty promises.

541
00:33:41,218 --> 00:33:45,139
Waiting is my biggest pet peeve.

542
00:33:57,693 --> 00:33:59,736
He even added corn.

543
00:33:59,736 --> 00:34:01,822
Managing the layout was the biggest challenge

544
00:34:01,822 --> 00:34:03,031
for this task.

545
00:34:03,031 --> 00:34:06,189
It was a straightforward approach for Han Lina.

546
00:34:06,189 --> 00:34:08,537
[Han Lina's Second Prime
After Working with Amy Choo?]

547
00:34:08,537 --> 00:34:10,664
Han Lina has completely bounced back.

548
00:34:10,664 --> 00:34:14,315
Apparently, this photoshoot led
to a series of acting contracts.

549
00:34:15,043 --> 00:34:17,462
Amy Choo never fails to impress.

550
00:34:17,462 --> 00:34:19,131
The most insane part is

551
00:34:19,131 --> 00:34:21,758
that Amy Choo actually mentioned your roommate.

552
00:34:21,758 --> 00:34:25,637
You credited an assistant
for the very first time in this spread.

553
00:34:25,637 --> 00:34:26,866
You mean Sun Tae Hyung?

554
00:34:26,866 --> 00:34:29,619
Yeah, he's been getting a lot of attention.

555
00:34:29,619 --> 00:34:32,811
[Photographer Amy Choo,
Assistant Sun Tae Hyung]

556
00:34:37,607 --> 00:34:39,799
Sun Tae Hyung.

557
00:34:42,672 --> 00:34:43,900
[Hey, you remember me, right?]

558
00:34:43,900 --> 00:34:46,010
If Amy Choo ever needs a new assistant,
you must bring me along!

559
00:34:46,010 --> 00:34:47,303
Come to Eunhasu
so we can have a celebration party.

560
00:34:47,303 --> 00:34:48,471
Danny, is this post actually referring to you?

561
00:34:48,471 --> 00:34:51,288
Did you actually become Amy Choo's assistant?

562
00:34:51,288 --> 00:34:53,499
Everyone is making such a big deal.

563
00:34:54,541 --> 00:34:57,085
Hey.

564
00:34:57,085 --> 00:34:58,545
Congratulations.

565
00:34:58,545 --> 00:35:00,797
Wait, you bought that?

566
00:35:00,797 --> 00:35:02,257
You, the cheapskate?

567
00:35:02,257 --> 00:35:03,467
Of course.

568
00:35:03,467 --> 00:35:05,802
He's collaborating with Amy Choo.

569
00:35:05,802 --> 00:35:08,911
Your uncle is amazing, isn't he?

570
00:35:11,016 --> 00:35:13,810
I'm curious,
do you actually know who Amy Choo is?

571
00:35:13,810 --> 00:35:15,062
Come on,

572
00:35:15,062 --> 00:35:17,481
Amy Choo is a household name.

573
00:35:17,481 --> 00:35:19,566
She collaborated with Baum Bag

574
00:35:19,566 --> 00:35:21,026
and received a prize in Berlin.

575
00:35:21,026 --> 00:35:22,986
What else?

576
00:35:22,986 --> 00:35:24,946
You looked her up beforehand, right?

577
00:35:24,946 --> 00:35:26,448
Just a bit.

578
00:35:26,448 --> 00:35:28,867
I'm at least familiar with the name.

579
00:35:28,867 --> 00:35:31,953
Why is my phone ringing so much today?

580
00:35:31,953 --> 00:35:33,330
Hello?

581
00:35:33,330 --> 00:35:35,540
You have a camera, right?

582
00:35:35,540 --> 00:35:37,460
Who's calling?

583
00:35:40,754 --> 00:35:42,464
Is this by any chance Amy Choo...

584
00:35:42,464 --> 00:35:43,298
Amy Choo?

585
00:35:43,298 --> 00:35:44,341
I've shared the location.

586
00:35:44,341 --> 00:35:46,760
Bring your preferred gear and show up tomorrow.

587
00:35:46,760 --> 00:35:48,680
What?

588
00:35:55,204 --> 00:35:56,520
You should head there tomorrow.

589
00:35:56,520 --> 00:35:58,563
I'm not going.
I already gave up on taking pictures.

590
00:35:58,563 --> 00:36:00,774
You were an award winner in school

591
00:36:00,774 --> 00:36:03,443
and made a name for yourself.

592
00:36:06,029 --> 00:36:08,615
People considered you a natural talent.

593
00:36:08,615 --> 00:36:09,991
How much longer will you shadow me?

594
00:36:09,991 --> 00:36:11,910
You should go there.

595
00:36:11,910 --> 00:36:14,663
Although I'm currently on leave,

596
00:36:14,663 --> 00:36:15,914
I have a job to return to,

597
00:36:15,914 --> 00:36:17,415
and I no longer own a camera.

598
00:36:17,415 --> 00:36:19,918
You do have a camera.

599
00:36:19,918 --> 00:36:22,462
The one you got as a birthday gift.

600
00:36:24,066 --> 00:36:25,382
The one you couldn't throw away

601
00:36:25,382 --> 00:36:26,591
because it was precious,

602
00:36:26,591 --> 00:36:28,760
so you picked it back up.

603
00:36:31,555 --> 00:36:33,807
I've tried

604
00:36:33,807 --> 00:36:37,249
to get rid of this, but I'm unable to.

605
00:36:38,520 --> 00:36:41,504
This isn't like me at all.

606
00:36:43,669 --> 00:36:47,802
Maybe it's because it was
my first and last birthday gift...

607
00:36:51,366 --> 00:36:53,952
Who was the sender?

608
00:36:54,786 --> 00:36:56,706
Someone.

609
00:36:58,748 --> 00:37:00,856
I just

610
00:37:02,002 --> 00:37:04,568
took photos of people and scenery

611
00:37:05,547 --> 00:37:08,425
while waiting

612
00:37:08,425 --> 00:37:11,178
for someone.

613
00:37:13,763 --> 00:37:17,331
I just took pictures whenever I missed them.

614
00:37:18,643 --> 00:37:21,021
I happen

615
00:37:21,021 --> 00:37:23,671
to be quite talented at it.

616
00:37:27,986 --> 00:37:31,303
I try to quit, but I keep shooting,

617
00:37:36,286 --> 00:37:39,353
and that only intensifies my longing.

618
00:37:40,916 --> 00:37:43,607
That's what this is.

619
00:37:44,711 --> 00:37:48,632
I really admired
that you had such a strong passion.

620
00:37:48,632 --> 00:37:51,051
You seemed

621
00:37:51,051 --> 00:37:54,179
quite impressive for once.

622
00:37:56,514 --> 00:37:59,434
If you need closure

623
00:37:59,434 --> 00:38:01,937
to understand why you can't let go,

624
00:38:01,937 --> 00:38:03,688
then go verify your feelings.

625
00:38:03,688 --> 00:38:05,941
Figure out if you're unable

626
00:38:05,941 --> 00:38:08,048
or unwilling to move on.

627
00:38:11,196 --> 00:38:12,197
And

628
00:38:12,197 --> 00:38:13,865
I'm willing to assist you

629
00:38:13,865 --> 00:38:16,243
in any way possible.

630
00:38:16,243 --> 00:38:19,537
- With what?
- With anything.

631
00:38:19,537 --> 00:38:21,915
It's a favor for the great pancakes

632
00:38:21,915 --> 00:38:23,856
you prepared yesterday.

633
00:38:29,881 --> 00:38:31,675
You should discover

634
00:38:31,675 --> 00:38:33,802
if it's attachment

635
00:38:33,802 --> 00:38:36,202
or genuine passion.

636
00:38:40,725 --> 00:38:44,168
Some things only become clear
once you've reached the end.

637
00:38:52,362 --> 00:38:54,572
Hey,

638
00:38:54,572 --> 00:38:56,825
can you leave work on time today?

639
00:38:56,825 --> 00:38:58,368
Hey.

640
00:38:58,368 --> 00:38:59,911
You've finally made a decision.

641
00:38:59,911 --> 00:39:01,496
I'm happy for you already.

642
00:39:01,496 --> 00:39:03,540
I'll make sure to leave on time today

643
00:39:03,540 --> 00:39:05,250
and be there by seven.

644
00:39:05,250 --> 00:39:07,127
Thank you.

645
00:39:07,127 --> 00:39:09,442
I won't break my word this time.

646
00:39:09,442 --> 00:39:11,384
[For an On-Time Exit]

647
00:39:27,541 --> 00:39:28,795
[Planning Team 3, First Report]

648
00:39:32,713 --> 00:39:34,473
[22 minutes]

649
00:39:36,489 --> 00:39:38,533
Yes.

650
00:39:38,533 --> 00:39:39,720
Hey.

651
00:39:39,720 --> 00:39:42,579
I'm ready to head out now.

652
00:39:42,579 --> 00:39:44,539
Really?

653
00:39:44,539 --> 00:39:46,458
Then how long will you be there?

654
00:39:46,458 --> 00:39:47,459
Yes.

655
00:39:47,459 --> 00:39:48,418
No.

656
00:39:48,418 --> 00:39:51,129
I'll adjust my schedule to make it work.

657
00:39:51,129 --> 00:39:52,964
In fact,

658
00:39:52,964 --> 00:39:54,884
it's definitely possible.

659
00:39:57,385 --> 00:39:59,054
Woo Hyun Jin.

660
00:39:59,054 --> 00:40:01,264
Can you stay out tonight?

661
00:40:01,264 --> 00:40:03,184
What?

662
00:40:05,894 --> 00:40:07,937
What should I do?

663
00:40:07,937 --> 00:40:09,230
It's me.

664
00:40:09,230 --> 00:40:10,357
I'm so sorry.

665
00:40:10,357 --> 00:40:12,650
An emergency occurred,

666
00:40:12,650 --> 00:40:14,402
so it looks like I'll be stuck at work.

667
00:40:14,402 --> 00:40:15,612
How can we fix this?

668
00:40:15,612 --> 00:40:17,155
Could you ask the neighbor for help?

669
00:40:17,155 --> 00:40:19,407
I'm deeply sorry for this.

670
00:40:19,407 --> 00:40:22,285
I feel sorry after encouraging you
for this chance.

671
00:40:22,285 --> 00:40:23,370
What should we do now?

672
00:40:23,370 --> 00:40:26,164
It's such an important day for you,

673
00:40:26,164 --> 00:40:27,665
and I've messed up big time.

674
00:40:27,665 --> 00:40:29,542
I'm truly sorry.

675
00:40:29,542 --> 00:40:31,252
Yeah,

676
00:40:31,252 --> 00:40:32,712
it can't be helped.

677
00:40:32,712 --> 00:40:34,297
You need to make it there at all costs.

678
00:40:34,297 --> 00:40:35,632
Definitely.

679
00:40:35,632 --> 00:40:38,115
I apologize again.

680
00:40:49,229 --> 00:40:52,421
Hey, what am I supposed to do now?

681
00:41:01,686 --> 00:41:04,170
Is this really the right way to do things?

682
00:41:06,351 --> 00:41:08,353
Hey.

683
00:41:08,353 --> 00:41:10,836
Would you like the front seat or the back seat?

684
00:41:14,901 --> 00:41:17,070
Hey.

685
00:41:17,070 --> 00:41:19,447
Why are you so fussy today?

686
00:41:19,447 --> 00:41:20,949
What's wrong?

687
00:41:20,949 --> 00:41:22,617
What's wrong with you?

688
00:41:22,617 --> 00:41:23,952
Come on,

689
00:41:23,952 --> 00:41:26,496
tell me.

690
00:41:26,496 --> 00:41:28,206
What?

691
00:41:28,206 --> 00:41:29,999
Is it because

692
00:41:29,999 --> 00:41:31,668
you don't have your bunny doll?

693
00:41:31,668 --> 00:41:34,526
Yeah, the bunny.

694
00:41:35,463 --> 00:41:36,422
Look.

695
00:41:36,422 --> 00:41:38,758
We're already here,

696
00:41:38,758 --> 00:41:41,094
so please be patient for just a little longer.

697
00:41:41,094 --> 00:41:43,014
Please.

698
00:41:49,727 --> 00:41:51,437
- You like this, right?
- Yeah.

699
00:41:51,437 --> 00:41:53,314
- You like it?
- Yes.

700
00:41:53,314 --> 00:41:55,441
Alright, help me out today.

701
00:41:55,441 --> 00:41:57,361
Yeah.

702
00:42:12,010 --> 00:42:13,754
Yes, Director,

703
00:42:13,754 --> 00:42:16,207
I'm on standby near the airport.

704
00:42:16,207 --> 00:42:18,295
I'll make this work no matter what.

705
00:42:18,295 --> 00:42:20,299
Understood.

706
00:42:25,164 --> 00:42:26,775
Do you still have that habit

707
00:42:26,775 --> 00:42:28,939
of framing things with data first?

708
00:42:28,939 --> 00:42:31,959
No, I've improved a lot.

709
00:42:32,851 --> 00:42:35,588
Remove slides 15 through 20 entirely.

710
00:42:35,588 --> 00:42:37,150
Clients care about the underlying framework

711
00:42:37,150 --> 00:42:39,258
rather than the emotional appeal.

712
00:43:34,788 --> 00:43:37,376
Are you done looking around?

713
00:43:41,420 --> 00:43:43,591
What's with the baby?

714
00:43:45,972 --> 00:43:48,864
There were some unavoidable circumstances.

715
00:43:48,864 --> 00:43:52,628
You're quite the source of diverse inspiration.

716
00:43:52,628 --> 00:43:54,687
Come on up.

717
00:43:59,315 --> 00:44:00,733
Keep eating that.

718
00:44:00,733 --> 00:44:02,653
Yeah.

719
00:44:05,445 --> 00:44:08,282
You're a bit different from that day.

720
00:44:08,282 --> 00:44:11,599
You were quite cocky back then.

721
00:44:13,870 --> 00:44:15,998
That was just some bravado

722
00:44:15,998 --> 00:44:18,083
for a temporary job. Today is different...

723
00:44:18,083 --> 00:44:20,794
Is the thought of seeing more of me

724
00:44:20,794 --> 00:44:23,361
making you feel a bit tense?

725
00:44:27,134 --> 00:44:29,054
Did you bring the item I asked for?

726
00:44:36,935 --> 00:44:38,312
It's a film camera.

727
00:44:38,312 --> 00:44:40,522
And it's an automatic?

728
00:44:40,522 --> 00:44:42,566
You've got quite the nerve.

729
00:44:42,566 --> 00:44:44,568
I got rid of all my gear three years ago,

730
00:44:44,568 --> 00:44:46,926
so this is all I have.

731
00:44:49,114 --> 00:44:51,700
I still really enjoy working with film,

732
00:44:51,700 --> 00:44:55,454
so I'm glad you brought one.

733
00:44:55,454 --> 00:44:58,457
It won't be a complex test.

734
00:44:58,457 --> 00:44:59,791
Alright.

735
00:44:59,791 --> 00:45:03,276
You have three hours to get the prints done.

736
00:45:06,381 --> 00:45:08,614
Just sit and wait.

737
00:45:26,401 --> 00:45:29,969
Some things only become clear
once you've reached the end.

738
00:45:41,792 --> 00:45:43,733
Hey, Woo Joo.

739
00:45:46,630 --> 00:45:48,882
These items are in a league of their own.

740
00:45:48,882 --> 00:45:50,008
If anything breaks,

741
00:45:50,008 --> 00:45:53,363
your aunt will be paying it off
until you're an adult.

742
00:45:55,639 --> 00:45:57,559
Stay here quietly. Okay?

743
00:46:03,897 --> 00:46:05,817
Okay.

744
00:46:06,525 --> 00:46:08,735
Come over here.

745
00:46:08,735 --> 00:46:10,696
Okay.

746
00:46:10,696 --> 00:46:13,115
I'll take a pretty picture of you,

747
00:46:13,115 --> 00:46:16,265
but after that, you have to stay still
and behave, okay?

748
00:46:39,723 --> 00:46:40,892
I've cleared the unnecessary slides

749
00:46:40,892 --> 00:46:43,334
and put the main info into a chart.

750
00:46:45,355 --> 00:46:48,422
It's been a while
since things were this hectic, Senior.

751
00:46:49,985 --> 00:46:52,635
Oh, I mean, Manager.

752
00:46:55,589 --> 00:46:58,118
Every detail of the layout,
including the margins, is flawless.

753
00:46:58,118 --> 00:47:00,454
Naturally, I learned from the best.

754
00:47:00,454 --> 00:47:03,396
I made sure
even the slide number alignment is perfect.

755
00:47:04,124 --> 00:47:09,110
It seems you're destined to be my manager,
both then and now.

756
00:47:13,965 --> 00:47:19,728
[Seorin University Joint Workshop
for Startup-Related Departments]

757
00:47:22,017 --> 00:47:24,686
Manager, give me ten minutes.

758
00:47:24,686 --> 00:47:27,022
I'm going to go give
those guys a piece of my mind.

759
00:47:27,022 --> 00:47:27,981
Hold on a second.

760
00:47:27,981 --> 00:47:29,900
Why is there always a family ritual
whenever we have a group assignment?

761
00:47:29,900 --> 00:47:31,234
I understand, but...

762
00:47:31,234 --> 00:47:33,028
That's such a weak excuse, isn't it?

763
00:47:33,028 --> 00:47:35,238
You're right, but wait.

764
00:47:35,238 --> 00:47:37,157
Why don't we sit for a moment?

765
00:47:37,157 --> 00:47:40,410
It's a weak excuse, but...

766
00:47:40,410 --> 00:47:41,912
It already looks good,

767
00:47:41,912 --> 00:47:46,498
but can we move this slightly to the right?

768
00:47:46,498 --> 00:47:48,710
That's a bit much.

769
00:47:48,710 --> 00:47:51,630
Who actually goes to the trouble
of balancing everything in a presentation?

770
00:47:51,630 --> 00:47:53,256
I see your point,

771
00:47:53,256 --> 00:47:55,634
but a chart might work better.

772
00:47:55,634 --> 00:47:59,744
Professor Kim has a preference
for official statistics and graphs.

773
00:48:00,889 --> 00:48:03,725
So, do you want this as a chart?

774
00:48:03,725 --> 00:48:05,435
Let's not stop there.

775
00:48:05,435 --> 00:48:06,269
Since it's a good concept,

776
00:48:06,269 --> 00:48:08,961
let's update everything.

777
00:48:10,649 --> 00:48:12,943
Understood. Okay.

778
00:48:12,943 --> 00:48:15,092
Geez.

779
00:48:17,072 --> 00:48:19,825
This really takes me back to our project days.

780
00:48:19,825 --> 00:48:20,784
We pulled all-nighters

781
00:48:20,784 --> 00:48:22,160
every single day

782
00:48:22,160 --> 00:48:23,787
just to win that scholarship.

783
00:48:23,787 --> 00:48:26,020
The scholarship wasn't my motivation.

784
00:48:28,583 --> 00:48:30,691
I stayed up for you.

785
00:48:33,797 --> 00:48:36,363
I simply wanted to be by your side all night.

786
00:49:09,497 --> 00:49:11,669
Woo Joo, how are you doing?

787
00:49:21,094 --> 00:49:23,014
Hey, Woo Joo.

788
00:49:32,606 --> 00:49:33,607
Help,

789
00:49:33,607 --> 00:49:36,109
the child has been injured.

790
00:49:36,109 --> 00:49:37,402
He had a fall

791
00:49:37,402 --> 00:49:40,822
and there's a lot of blood right here.

792
00:49:40,822 --> 00:49:42,741
This wound requires stitches.

793
00:49:42,741 --> 00:49:45,160
He'll need a local anesthetic.

794
00:49:45,160 --> 00:49:48,018
Are you the guardian?

795
00:49:49,122 --> 00:49:51,541
You must be accompanied by a guardian.

796
00:49:51,541 --> 00:49:53,585
Doctor.

797
00:49:53,585 --> 00:49:55,505
Just a second.

798
00:50:05,178 --> 00:50:08,105
[Temporary helper]

799
00:50:16,358 --> 00:50:18,318
Why isn't she picking up?

800
00:50:18,318 --> 00:50:21,277
Your call is being forwarded to voicemail...

801
00:50:21,277 --> 00:50:23,071
Please. The honor's mine.

802
00:50:23,071 --> 00:50:24,989
I have high expectations for your company.

803
00:50:24,989 --> 00:50:25,865
Thanks.

804
00:50:25,865 --> 00:50:27,241
We hope to see you again soon.

805
00:50:27,241 --> 00:50:27,992
Thank you.

806
00:50:27,992 --> 00:50:30,127
- Take care.
- Take care.

807
00:50:40,338 --> 00:50:41,967
[Missed call]

808
00:50:41,967 --> 00:50:43,887
Oh, he called.

809
00:50:46,214 --> 00:50:47,263
Where are you right now?

810
00:50:47,263 --> 00:50:48,515
Why haven't you been picking up?

811
00:50:48,515 --> 00:50:51,351
Well, work suddenly came up...

812
00:50:51,351 --> 00:50:52,769
Forget that,

813
00:50:52,769 --> 00:50:54,771
the baby is in the hospital.

814
00:50:54,771 --> 00:50:57,480
The hospital?

815
00:50:57,480 --> 00:50:58,525
What's wrong?

816
00:50:58,525 --> 00:50:59,359
What happened?

817
00:50:59,359 --> 00:51:01,820
I need to head somewhere else urgently.

818
00:51:01,820 --> 00:51:03,071
Where is the location?

819
00:51:03,071 --> 00:51:05,137
I'll drive you there.

820
00:51:10,328 --> 00:51:11,997
I'm Sun Woo Joo's guardian.

821
00:51:11,997 --> 00:51:13,289
Where is he?

822
00:51:13,289 --> 00:51:15,209
Please wait a second.

823
00:51:51,453 --> 00:51:53,373
Tae Hyung.

824
00:51:54,205 --> 00:51:56,583
I'm so sorry.

825
00:51:56,583 --> 00:51:58,293
I feel terrible about the interview,

826
00:51:58,293 --> 00:52:00,901
and for making you wait
so long at the hospital too.

827
00:52:07,302 --> 00:52:09,137
By the way,

828
00:52:09,137 --> 00:52:11,829
how exactly did he get injured?

829
00:52:13,016 --> 00:52:15,332
Why haven't I been able to get a hold of you?

830
00:52:19,355 --> 00:52:21,441
I'm sorry.

831
00:52:21,441 --> 00:52:23,799
Things have been so hectic for me...

832
00:52:29,866 --> 00:52:32,992
I was lost

833
00:52:32,992 --> 00:52:35,330
because they wouldn't perform the procedure
without a guardian,

834
00:52:35,330 --> 00:52:37,999
and you weren't picking up.

835
00:52:37,999 --> 00:52:40,482
I was going to lose my mind the whole time.

836
00:52:45,799 --> 00:52:47,759
I told you I hate waiting.

837
00:52:47,759 --> 00:52:49,010
How many times has this happened already?

838
00:52:49,010 --> 00:52:50,637
You should just...

839
00:52:50,637 --> 00:52:53,765
not make promises you can't keep.

840
00:52:53,765 --> 00:52:55,058
Tae Hyung.

841
00:52:55,058 --> 00:52:56,726
I really am trying my best
to take responsibility...

842
00:52:56,726 --> 00:52:58,561
For whom?

843
00:52:58,561 --> 00:52:59,729
Who is taking responsibility for whom?

844
00:52:59,729 --> 00:53:01,481
You can't even handle your own life,

845
00:53:01,481 --> 00:53:04,548
much less a baby.

846
00:53:11,116 --> 00:53:12,826
You are no different.

847
00:53:12,826 --> 00:53:14,869
If you said you would look after him,
you should have done a better job.

848
00:53:14,869 --> 00:53:17,622
Didn't I make it clear?

849
00:53:17,622 --> 00:53:20,773
I'm not the kind of person
who should be in charge of anyone.

850
00:53:21,543 --> 00:53:23,753
Snap out of it.

851
00:53:23,753 --> 00:53:26,005
I'm not the parent,

852
00:53:26,005 --> 00:53:27,841
you are.

853
00:53:27,841 --> 00:53:29,865
You're the one

854
00:53:31,136 --> 00:53:34,620
who stepped up to take him in, not me.

855
00:53:37,934 --> 00:53:40,501
Is Sun Woo Joo's guardian here?

856
00:53:47,485 --> 00:53:50,405
Luckily, it's just a minor cut.

857
00:53:50,405 --> 00:53:54,784
Please return in five days
to get the stitches out.

858
00:53:54,784 --> 00:53:56,077
That said,

859
00:53:56,077 --> 00:53:57,996
has he been

860
00:53:57,996 --> 00:54:00,832
struggling with sleep?

861
00:54:00,832 --> 00:54:02,375
Is he waking up at odd hours

862
00:54:02,375 --> 00:54:05,003
or acting up during the day?

863
00:54:05,003 --> 00:54:08,047
I haven't tracked it recently,

864
00:54:08,047 --> 00:54:09,257
but he's usually a deep sleeper...

865
00:54:09,257 --> 00:54:10,633
Actually,

866
00:54:10,633 --> 00:54:13,636
he's been waking up
every fifteen minutes lately.

867
00:54:13,636 --> 00:54:14,971
If he's left alone,

868
00:54:14,971 --> 00:54:18,224
he wakes up crying in less than ten minutes.

869
00:54:18,224 --> 00:54:21,811
It's likely an emotional response to stress.

870
00:54:21,811 --> 00:54:23,438
That major incident from before

871
00:54:23,438 --> 00:54:26,983
is probably the trigger.

872
00:54:26,983 --> 00:54:29,777
Right now, his mental state

873
00:54:29,777 --> 00:54:32,739
is more concerning than the cut.

874
00:54:32,739 --> 00:54:34,616
Even at his age,

875
00:54:34,616 --> 00:54:37,076
children sense everything.

876
00:54:37,076 --> 00:54:41,436
You need to take extra care of him.

877
00:54:53,259 --> 00:54:54,928
Thank goodness.

878
00:54:54,928 --> 00:54:57,035
The fever has gone down.

879
00:55:02,769 --> 00:55:05,438
Woo Joo.

880
00:55:05,438 --> 00:55:07,629
Forgive me.

881
00:55:08,274 --> 00:55:12,050
For not being there with you yesterday.

882
00:55:13,446 --> 00:55:15,949
I love you.

883
00:55:15,949 --> 00:55:18,015
Me too.

884
00:55:21,246 --> 00:55:23,437
Wait a minute.

885
00:55:35,176 --> 00:55:37,826
Is his temperature back to normal?

886
00:55:40,265 --> 00:55:42,016
Yeah.

887
00:55:42,016 --> 00:55:44,833
Then, well, it's fine.

888
00:56:01,452 --> 00:56:03,372
Woo Joo.

889
00:56:07,417 --> 00:56:10,795
Your uncle must have been really scared.

890
00:56:10,795 --> 00:56:12,715
Right?

891
00:56:21,554 --> 00:56:22,890
Who is taking responsibility for whom?

892
00:56:22,890 --> 00:56:24,809
You can't even handle your own life,

893
00:56:24,809 --> 00:56:28,126
much less a baby.

894
00:56:29,647 --> 00:56:32,608
Why did I have to say that?

895
00:56:32,608 --> 00:56:34,633
Darn it.

896
00:56:35,903 --> 00:56:38,679
Why was I so dramatic?

897
00:56:44,869 --> 00:56:45,621
Hello.

898
00:56:45,621 --> 00:56:47,729
Hello. Welcome.

899
00:56:52,045 --> 00:56:54,797
It's for a 20-month-old kid,

900
00:56:54,797 --> 00:56:56,090
so he can eat abalone porridge, right?

901
00:56:56,090 --> 00:56:57,008
Sure.

902
00:56:57,008 --> 00:56:59,093
I'll take the premium one.

903
00:56:59,093 --> 00:57:00,470
Alright.

904
00:57:00,470 --> 00:57:02,555
And,

905
00:57:02,555 --> 00:57:04,182
something for an adult to eat,

906
00:57:04,182 --> 00:57:06,373
please recommend something.

907
00:57:16,110 --> 00:57:19,011
I look like a mess.

908
00:57:52,563 --> 00:57:54,483
You're here?

909
00:57:56,401 --> 00:58:00,154
I'm going to eat ramen.

910
00:58:00,154 --> 00:58:02,429
Do you want to eat together?

911
00:58:04,534 --> 00:58:07,161
I picked up some porridge,

912
00:58:07,161 --> 00:58:09,747
let's share this.

913
00:58:09,747 --> 00:58:11,667
Okay.

914
00:58:17,255 --> 00:58:19,175
Who is it?

915
00:58:22,535 --> 00:58:24,011
What?

916
00:58:24,011 --> 00:58:26,305
What is the manager doing here...

917
00:58:26,305 --> 00:58:28,349
Hello, I'm the landlord of unit 206.

918
00:58:28,349 --> 00:58:29,809
Landlord?

919
00:58:29,809 --> 00:58:31,686
He's the landlord?

920
00:58:31,686 --> 00:58:34,315
- Of this house?
- Yes.

921
00:59:20,822 --> 00:59:23,822
Senior, you're the landlord here, right?

922
00:59:23,822 --> 00:59:25,197
Senior?

923
00:59:25,197 --> 00:59:27,655
Can you believe I actually
crossed paths with her first love?

924
00:59:27,655 --> 00:59:29,946
Can someone tell me what has got him so angry?

925
00:59:29,946 --> 00:59:31,330
Do you want to go camping tomorrow?

926
00:59:31,330 --> 00:59:33,030
- Say "ah."
- I said I don't want any.

927
00:59:33,030 --> 00:59:33,787
- Tae Hyung.
- Excuse me.

928
00:59:33,787 --> 00:59:34,747
It's awkward, I know.

929
00:59:34,747 --> 00:59:36,322
But we're practically strangers,
so of course it is.

930
00:59:36,322 --> 00:59:38,697
Shall we try to get close like before?

931
00:59:38,697 --> 00:59:39,863
- Your wife?
- Excuse me?

932
00:59:39,863 --> 00:59:41,128
No, she isn't.

933
00:59:41,128 --> 00:59:42,863
However, the camera lens never lies.

934
00:59:42,863 --> 00:59:44,381
The way you are gazing at her,

935
00:59:44,381 --> 00:59:46,238
and the emotions you felt
while taking that picture,

936
00:59:46,238 --> 00:59:48,977
that kind of shot is impossible without love.
